    "content": {
      "value": "Overview\n--------\n\nEditorial and CMS content in the Zimmermann SFCC platform is owned by Contentful and managed by the Zimmermann content team. MRT (Managed Runtime — Salesforce's PWA hosting layer) acts as the integration layer between Contentful and the browser-rendered PWA storefront.\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Direction** | **Flow** |\n| Inbound (Contentful → MRT) | Published content entries (hero banners, editorial modules, navigation, footer, announcement banners, size guides, accordion copy) delivered via the Contentful Delivery API (CDA). Target: fetched server-side by the MRT SSR layer. Current: fetched client-side post-hydration. |\n| Outbound (MRT → Contentful) | Cache-purge webhook acknowledgements; Management API calls from CI for schema migrations. No content flows from SFCC back to Contentful. |\n| NOT in this flow | SFCC does not connect to Contentful directly. All CMS content is fetched by the MRT Node layer, not by SFCC cartridges or Business Manager. |\n\n*Contentful is the sole CMS for all eight Zimmermann storefronts. SFCC manages commerce data (products, pricing, orders); Contentful manages editorial data (copy, imagery configuration, page layouts). They complement each other without overlap.*\n\nIntegration Architecture & Data Flow\n------------------------------------\n\n**Pattern:** Contentful → MRT (Node/SSR) → browser.\n\n### Architecture diagram\n\nwide760PWA (SSR layer, then CSR hydration)\n│\n├──► Contentful Delivery API (CDA) — published content\n│ SSR fetches server-side; browser also uses CDA on\n│ post-hydration reads. Public token, safe in bundle.\n│\n├──► Contentful Preview API (CPA) — draft content\n│ Editor preview only. Token held server-side in MRT;\n│ never reaches the browser. Requests proxied through\n│ an MRT preview endpoint.\n│\n├──► Contentful Images API (images.ctfassets.net)\n│ srcset / sizes / avif|webp / quality parameters\n│\n└──◄ Publish webhook → MRT /webhooks/contentful\nClears affected SSR cache keys on entry publish.\nHMAC-verified with a shared secret.\n\n### **API surface & token boundary**\n\n| Surface | Origin / Boundary | Token | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| CDA (published) | Browser + SSR | `CONTENTFUL_DELIVERY_TOKEN` (public, read-only) | Safe to embed in bundle. |\n| CPA (drafts) | MRT proxy only | `CONTENTFUL_PREVIEW_TOKEN` (server-side) | Editor preview via iframe `postMessage`. Never reaches browser. |\n| CMA (schema sync) | CI host only | `CONTENTFUL_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN` | Never in MRT/bundle — build-time only. Never embedded, never in PR diffs. |\n| Publish webhook | Contentful → MRT | `CMS_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (HMAC) | Clears SSR cache keys on publish. TTL fallback 60s SWR. Rejected and logged if HMAC fails. |\n\n#### Current state (built today)\n\nThese are confirmed by the code in the repo as of this spike.\n\n| What | File | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| CDA fetch hook | `overrides/app/hooks/useContentful.ts` | `useContentfulEntries` and `useContentfulEntry` — **client-side only** (`useEffect`). Fires in the browser after hydration, not during SSR. |\n| Homepage Contentful fetch | `overrides/app/pages/home/index.tsx` | Calls `useContentfulEntries('homepage')` in `HomeNormal` — CSR via `useEffect`. |\n| Live preview (Studio) | `pages/home/index.tsx` + `useContentfulLiveUpdates` | Preview path wired via `?entry=` param. Uses `@contentful/live-preview/react`. |\n| Editorial components | `overrides/app/components/contentful/` | `heroBanner`, `productHero`, `duplexSection`, `videoEmbed` |\n| Studio Experience components | `overrides/app/components/contentful/experiences/` | `CollectionHero`, `ImageText`, `ShoppableImage` registered via `definitions.ts` |\n| Studio Experience route | `overrides/app/pages/experience/index.tsx` | — |\n| Config & types | `overrides/app/config/contentful.ts`, `config/contentfulMapping.ts`, `types/contentful.ts` | Token config resolved from MRT `getConfig()` |\n| Schema-as-code tooling | `scripts/contentful/sync.js`, `generateDefinitions.mjs`, `migrations/`, `setup/bootstrapSpace.mjs` | — |\n| CSP allowances | `overrides/app/ssr/contentSecurityPolicy.ts` | `cdn.contentful.com`, `preview.contentful.com`, `images.ctfassets.net`, `frame-ancestors: app.contentful.com` |\n\n#### Target architecture (to build)\n\nThese are the intended production patterns. **None of these exist in the codebase yet.** Squads must not assume they are live.\n\n| What | Why it's needed | Build reference |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| SSR-first CDA fetch | Editorial content for SEO/LCP-critical pages (homepage, PLP, PDP) must be fetched server-side. Currently `useContentful.ts` fires in the browser — first paint shows a spinner, not content. Target: SSR fetches CDA, browser hydrates from SSR payload with no CDA call on first paint. | Replace `useEffect` fetch with server-side data loading in the MRT SSR layer. |\n| GraphQL Content API | For composed pages that assemble multiple entries, a single GraphQL query fetches only the needed fields, avoiding multiple REST round-trips and over-fetching. Currently all fetches use REST CDA (`cdn.contentful.com/.../entries`). | Introduce a GraphQL client (e.g. `graphql-request`) and query layer per content type. |\n| HMAC-verified publish webhook receiver | When an editor publishes in Contentful Studio, the MRT SSR cache must be purged immediately. Without this, content changes won't appear until the 60s TTL expires. Currently no webhook endpoint exists in `overrides/` or `scripts/`. | Build a `POST /webhooks/contentful` handler in the MRT Node layer. Verify `X-Contentful-Signature` against `CMS_WEBHOOK_SECRET`. |\n\n### Content Ownership (from 02-contentful.md)\n\nSFCC owns all commerce data; Contentful owns editorial. On pages that mix both, editorial comes from Contentful and commerce data is resolved from SFCC. Product and category references in Contentful entries are authored via the Salesforce Commerce Cloud Connector app and resolved at render (HPC-001).\n\n| **Surface** | **SFCC Owns** | **Contentful Owns** | **Status** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Homepage | Commerce data for embedded product refs | All modules — hero, banners, campaign blocks | Confirmed |\n| Campaign landing pages | Commerce data for embedded product refs | Full page (Contentful Studio Experiences) | Confirmed |\n| Lookbooks | Commerce data for shop-the-look refs | Imagery, layout, copy | Confirmed |\n| Size guides | — | Fallback content only. Primary size guide is Measmerize overlay (PRD-053). Contentful serves size guide content only where no Measmerize data exists. | Confirmed |\n| Footer | — | All content | Confirmed |\n| PLP / category | Category results, product tiles, facets, pagination, hero/banner and editorial rows (SFCC BM — SPR-03/04/64) | Contentful-authored editorial rows, if any | Pending — whether any PLP editorial comes from Contentful |\n| PDP | Product attributes, price, inventory, variations, gallery | Marketing copy, editorial blocks, size guide fallback (primary is Measmerize — PRD-053) | Pending — which blocks are Contentful vs SFCC Page Designer |\n| Navigation / mega-menu | Category tree | Promotional tiles, if any | Pending |\n| Product badges | Badge labels and taxonomy — managed in SFCC BM product attributes (PRD-005) | — | Confirmed — Contentful is not the source of badge content |\n\nSFCC Product & Category ID Reference Pattern in Contentful\n----------------------------------------------------------\n\nThis section documents the resolved design for how SFCC product and category IDs are embedded in Contentful content models, how MRT resolves them at render time, and how conditional component rendering is implemented based on those IDs. This is the core design question the spike(SFCC-123) was tasked to answer.\n\n### Content Model: How to Store SFCC IDs\n\nSFCC product and category IDs are stored as plain Short Text fields on the Contentful content type. They are not localized — they are structural fields that identify what SFCC data the editorial entry is associated with, and the value does not change per locale.\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Field Name** | **Field Type** | **Localized** | **Applies To** | **Description** |\n| sfccCategoryId | Short Text | No | PLP editorial slots, Inline Grid Insert, Mega Menu tiles | The SFCC category ID (e.g. womens-dresses) this entry is scoped to. If null, the entry is shown on all categories of that type. |\n| sfccProductId | Short Text | No | PDP editorial blocks, Shop the Look | The SFCC product ID (master product ID) this entry is scoped to. If null, shown on all PDPs. |\n| sfccProductIds | Short Text (list) | No | Campaign editorial, Homepage personalisation | Array of SFCC product IDs when an entry targets multiple products. |\n| sfccCategoryIds | Short Text (list) | No | Multi-category editorial slots | Array of SFCC category IDs when an entry targets multiple categories. |\n\n*Authoring rule: content authors set sfccCategoryId / sfccProductId in Contentful. They do not need to know anything about how MRT resolves it — that logic lives entirely in the SSR layer.*\n\n### Schema-as-Code Definition\n\nEach content type that supports ID-based targeting must include the relevant field in its scripts/contentful/content-types/\\*.js definition. Example for PLP Inline Grid Insert:\n\nwide760true{\nid: 'sfccCategoryId',\nname: 'SFCC Category ID',\ntype: 'Symbol',          // Short Text in Contentful UI\nlocalized: false,\nrequired: false,\nvalidations: []\n}\n\n### Render-Time Resolution in MRT (SSR)\n\nAt SSR time, MRT fetches all published entries of a given content type for the current locale via CDA. Before passing entries to React components, the SSR layer filters them by matching the SFCC ID field against the current page context. The component never sees unmatched entries — it receives only the entries that should render.\n\n**Resolution logic by page context:**\n\n|  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Page Context** | **ID Source** | **Match Logic** |\n| PLP (category page) | Route param / SFCC category API response | Filter CDA entries where sfccCategoryId === currentCategoryId OR sfccCategoryId is null (show-on-all). |\n| PDP (product page) | Route param productId (master product ID) | Filter CDA entries where sfccProductId === currentProductId OR sfccProductId is null. |\n| Homepage | No SFCC ID context | No ID filtering — all entries for the slot are rendered in authored order. |\n| Campaign landing | Slug / experience ID | Filtered by Contentful Studio Experience — no SFCC ID filtering needed. |\n\n**Pseudocode — MRT SSR filter (PLP example):**\n\nconst allGridInserts = await contentfulClient.getEntries({   content\\_type: 'plpInlineGridInsert',   locale: currentLocale, });  const matchedInserts = allGridInserts.items.filter(entry => {   const { sfccCategoryId } = entry.fields;   // null = show on all categories; specific ID = scoped render   return !sfccCategoryId || sfccCategoryId === currentCategoryId; });  // Only matched entries are passed to the component return <PlpInlineGridInsert entries={matchedInserts} />;\n\n### Cache Key Requirements\n\nThis is a critical implication of the ID-based filtering pattern. If SSR cache keys do not include the SFCC category or product ID, the cached response for one category will be incorrectly served to a different category.\n\n*Cache key rule: any page whose SSR output depends on sfccCategoryId filtering MUST include the category ID in its MRT cache key. Same rule applies to sfccProductId on PDPs. Failure to do this will cause editorial components to appear on the wrong category/product pages.*\n\n**Cache key construction:**\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Page** | **Cache Key Must Include** |\n| PLP | locale + categoryId + (page number if paginated) |\n| PDP | locale + productId |\n| Homepage | locale only (no SFCC ID context) |\n\n### Component Contract\n\nReact components that render SFCC-ID-targeted content must be written to the following contract:\n\n* The component does NOT receive raw Contentful entries — it receives pre-filtered entries from the SSR layer.\n* The component does NOT contain any SFCC ID comparison logic.\n* The component renders all entries it receives, in the order it receives them.\n* If the entries array is empty (no match), the component renders nothing — null return, no DOM output.\n\nThis keeps the component reusable across different SFCC ID scopes without modification.\n\n### Null / Unscoped Behaviour\n\nA Contentful entry with sfccCategoryId = null (field left empty by the author) is treated as \"show on all categories\" for that content type. This is the default authoring state. Authors only populate the ID field when they want to restrict the component to a specific category or product.\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **sfccCategoryId value** | **Render behaviour** |\n| null (empty) | Show on all PLPs of this content type |\n| \"womens-dresses\" | Show only on the womens-dresses PLP |\n| \"mens-shirts\" | Show only on the mens-shirts PLP |\n\nContent Model Requirements\n--------------------------\n\n### SPRINT 1 Content Types — Required Now\n\nDerived from active and blocked Jira stories. Each type requires a TypeScript React component in overrides/ and a schema definition in scripts/contentful/content-types/\\*.js.\n\n|  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Content Type** | **Required By** | **Key Fields** | **Locale** |\n| Promotional Announcement Banner | [SFCC-51](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-51) (Blocked), [SFCC-111](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-111) | messages[], CTA link, rotation timing, page visibility, position, per-customer-group config, scheduling (start/end), enabled flag | Yes — per storefront |\n| Global Footer | [SFCC-55](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-55), [SFCC-117](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-117) | nav link columns, legal/copyright text, region-specific links (e.g. AU Acknowledgement of Country), bottom bar | Yes — per storefront |\n| Homepage — Hero Banner | [SFCC-90](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-90), [SFCC-58](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-58) | image, headline, subheadline, CTA link, full-bleed vs padded variant | Yes |\n| Homepage — Content Row / Image Grid | [SFCC-94](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-94) | images[], column count (2/3/4), CTA link per image, carousel flag | Yes |\n| Homepage — Editorial Feature Block | [SFCC-90](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-90) | editorial image, title, body copy, CTA link, optional product tile link | Yes |\n| Navigation / Mega Menu | [SFCC-96](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-96), [SFCC-52](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-52) | top-level nav items[], subcategory links[], editorial image slot (optional), per-storefront cloneable - provisional, pending SFCC-96 Figma spec | Yes — per storefront |\n\n### SPRINT 2 Content Types\n\n|  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Content Type** | **Required By** | **Key Fields** | **Locale** |\n| Size Guide | [SFCC-102](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-102) | size guide content per product type, images/table data | Yes |\n| PLP Bottom Zone Editorial Slots | [SFCC-82](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-82) | full-width image block, editorial feature block, two-column content block — each with image, title, copy, CTA | Yes |\n| PLP Inline Grid Insert | [SFCC-190](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-190) | campaignImage, editorialText (optional), featuredProductTile (optional), position, sfccCategoryId (Short Text, localized: false). Conditional render: MRT SSR filters entries by sfccCategoryId vs current route categoryId. Pending [SFCC-238](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-238) — PLP grid injection and pagination/item-count behaviour to be confirmed before build begins. See [SFCC-238](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-238). | Yes |\n| PDP Accordion Content | [SFCC-195](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-195) | accordionLabel, bodyCopy (rich text) per storefront (Shipping & Returns, Assistance). Details & Care and Size & Fit: SFCC-sourced. sfccProductId (Short Text, localized: false) — scopes accordion overrides to a specific product. Mixed content resolution (Contentful tabs + SFCC tabs) proposed, not yet resolved: Contentful tabs (Shipping & Returns, Assistance) render via rich-text renderer; SFCC tabs (Details & Care, Size & Fit) are SFCC-sourced — exact rendering mechanism (simple SFCC variable call vs. dedicated component) still TBC, pending a spike (no card raised yet — see Capability Build Table). | Yes — per storefront |\n\n### Identified — Sprint TBD\n\n|  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Content Type** | **Jira** | **Target Sprint** | **Notes** |\n| Z.immerse editorial page templates | [SFCC-10](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-10) | Sprint 5 | Full flexible component library. Content model needs design before build. |\n| Mini-cart Shop the Look | [SFCC-11](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-11) | TBD | Editorial content slot inside mini-cart. |\n| FAQ / Article structured data | [SFCC-173](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-173) | TBD | JSON-LD schema enrichment for GEO/AI Overviews. |\n| Homepage personalisation (authenticated) | [SFCC-160](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-160) | Year 2 | Full Contentful personalisation — pending contract timeline. |\n| Countdown timer module | [SFCC-162](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-162) | TBD | Could Have — pending design confirmation. |\n| Checkout Trust Messaging | [SFCC-67](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-67) | Sprint 4 | Sits under Checkout Flow & Delivery epic. Field set TBD at sprint planning. |\n| Returns / Refund Messaging | [SFCC-14](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-14) | Sprint 7 | SFCC-14 is an Epic — build to child story once raised. Fields TBD. |\n\n### What is NOT in Contentful\n\nDo not model these in Contentful — owned by other systems:\n\n* Product data (names, descriptions, pricing, stock) — AP21 → MuleSoft → SFCC\n* Product imagery — pending decision on DC002 (Product Images Location); PWA TSD indicates Contentful, Product TSD indicates SFCC BM, not yet reconciled\n* Orders, customer data, basket — SFCC / NewStore / Omneo\n* Tax rules, pricebooks, checkout configuration — SFCC Business Manager\n* GTM tags, analytics configuration — Tell No Lies\n\nSFCC-Side Consumption & Build Scope\n-----------------------------------\n\n### **Already built:**\n\n* Config/types: overrides/app/config/contentful.ts · config/contentfulMapping.ts · types/contentful.ts\n* Data hook: overrides/app/hooks/useContentful.ts\n* Components: components/contentful/{heroBanner, productHero, duplexSection, videoEmbed}.tsx\n* Studio Experiences: components/contentful/experiences/{shoppableImage.tsx, definitions.ts} · pages/experience/index.tsx\n* Schema-as-code + tooling: scripts/contentful/{sync.js, generateDefinitions.mjs, migrations/}\n* Runtime: CSP allowances in overrides/app/ssr/contentSecurityPolicy.ts · Studio registration via .claude/skills/contentful-register-component\n\n### Capability Build Table\n\n| **Capability** | **APIs / Fields Consumed** | **Rendering Logic** | **Status** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Promotional Announcement Banner | CDA: messages[], ctaLink, rotationInterval, enabled, scheduledStart/End, position, customerGroup, enabledPages | Rotate client-side. Suppress if enabled=false or outside schedule. Match customerGroup vs SFCC session. | To build — [SFCC-51](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-51) blocked |\n| Homepage — Hero Banner | CDA: image (Asset), headline, subheadline, ctaText, ctaLink, variant (full-bleed|padded) | SSR as <h1>. Image via Contentful Images API w=1920&fm=webp. Omit CTA if null. | To build — [SFCC-90](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-90) |\n| Homepage — Content Row / Image Grid | CDA: images[] (Assets), columnCount (2/3/4), ctaLink per image, carouselFlag | Grid or carousel by columnCount. All images via Contentful Images API. | To build — [SFCC-94](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-94) |\n| Homepage — Editorial Feature Block | CDA: image, title, bodyCopy, ctaLink, productTileLink (optional) | SSR render. Omit product tile if null. | To build — [SFCC-90](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-90) |\n| Navigation / Mega Menu | CDA: navItems[] (label, link, hasMegaMenu, subcategories[], editorialImage, editorialLink) | Preserve Contentful item order. No dropdown if hasMegaMenu=false. | To build — [SFCC-96](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-96) |\n| Global Footer | CDA: navLinkColumns[], legalText, regionLinks[], bottomBar | SSR. Region-specific links filtered by SFCC site ID. | To build — [SFCC-55](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-55) |\n| PLP Bottom Zone Editorial Slots | CDA: fullWidthImageBlock, editorialFeatureBlock, twoColumnContentBlock | Render below PLP grid. Locale-aware. | To build — [SFCC-82](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-82) |\n| PLP Inline Grid Insert | CDA: campaignImage, editorialText (optional), featuredProductTile (optional), position, sfccCategoryId | MRT SSR filters all entries of this type by sfccCategoryId vs currentCategoryId (route param). Null sfccCategoryId = show on all categories. Inject matched entries into grid at configured position. Cache key must include categoryId. | To build — [SFCC-190](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-190) Pending [SFCC-238](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-238) — grid injection without breaking item counts or pagination to be confirmed before build begins. |\n| PDP Size Guide Fallback | CDA: sizeGuideContent per product type, images/table data | Show only when Measmerize returns no data for the product (PRD-053). | To build — [SFCC-102](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-102) |\n| PDP Accordion Content | CDA: accordionLabel,  bodyCopy (rich text) - per storefront (Shipping & Returns, Assistance tabs only).  sfccProductId - scopes entry to specific product Details & Care and Size & Fit: SFCC-sourced fields (exact fields TBD - pending spike).   EU-only: Environmental Qualities tab conditional on AP21 attribute (PRD-009) | Render as accordion tabs. Shipping & Returns and Assistance tabs: rich text via Contentful rich-text renderer. Details & Care and Size & Fit tabs: SFCC-sourced — rendering approach TBD (simple SFCC variable call vs dedicated component — spike required). EU-only Environmental Qualities tab (PRD-009): renders only when AP21 attribute is populated; suppressed for non-EU storefronts. | In Refinement — [SFCC-195](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-195)  Spike needed: mixed content rendering (Contentful + SFCC tabs) inside accordion body. No card raised yet — raise a spike or confirm scope with SFCC-238 before build begins. |\n| Checkout Trust Messaging | CDA: trustMessageBlocks[], collectInBoutiqueDisclaimer, deliveryDisclaimer — per storefront | Render in checkout flow. | To build — [SFCC-67](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-67) (Sprint 4 — Checkout Flow & Delivery epic) |\n| Returns / Refund Messaging | TBD | TBD | Blocked — [SFCC-14](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-14) is an Epic(Sprint 7). Update once child story is created. |\n\nError Handling & Monitoring\n---------------------------\n\n### Scope Boundary — What Squad A/B Commits To vs Recommendations\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Area** | **Position** |\n| In-code null-safe rendering | Squad A/B commits — defensive React code, part of building each component. |\n| HMAC verification on webhook | Squad A/B commits — part of building the webhook receiver endpoint. |\n| Graceful degradation (CDA down) | Squad A/B commits — already listed as a build checklist [item](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/346783750/Contentful+Integration+Technical+Design+Content+Model+SFCC-249#PWA-Integration). |\n| Writing to MRT log drain (Node layer only) | Squad A/B commits — server-side logging from the MRT Node layer. No browser-side New Relic events or PWA kit instrumentation in scope for this integration. |\n| Browser-side PWA kit events / custom New Relic instrumentation | **Out of Squad A/B scope for this integration.** The New Relic Browser Agent is documented in the PDP integrations page (INT-032) but is currently marked as **Not Required / P2**, with licence type and sampling approach still unresolved. If confirmed as required, raise as a separate story. Note: `SENTRY_DSN` is also a configured MRT env var per the PWA TSD — confirm which tool owns browser-layer error reporting before wiring either. |\n| New Relic log drain setup per MRT environment | Not Squad A/B — tracked as a checklist item in CDN, eCDN, and Security Configuration pages. Must be complete before any alert policies function. It is a prerequisite, not a task for Squad A/B. |\n| Alert policy creation and tuning in New Relic | Recommendation only — per Accenture Observability shared responsibility model. Squad A/B provides the recommended thresholds; the owning team creates and tunes them. |\n| New Relic dashboard for content team warnings | Recommendation only — confirm whether this falls under the Observability shared responsibility model or needs a separate request to the content team's tooling owner. |\n| Sentry vs New Relic — browser layer | Both SENTRY\\_DSN and NEW\\_RELIC\\_LICENSE\\_KEY are established MRT env vars per the PWA TSD. Confirm with integration lead or DevOps which tool owns browser-layer error reporting to avoid duplication. |\n\n### Scenario Table\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Scenario** | **Handling (Squad A/B)** | **Logging (Squad A/B)** | **Incident / Alert** | **Owner** |\n| Contentful CDA unavailable during SSR | Serve stale SSR cache within the SWR window. Fall back to a bare page render if the cache is cold. Never block page rendering due to CMS unavailability.   Note: Footer and homepage lack an editorial-free fallback—a bare render produces a visually broken page; this risk is accepted during a full CDA outage. | Log errors with scenario ID, affected route, and CDA response status to the MRT log drain. | New Relic alert policy fires if CDA error rate exceeds 5% of SSR requests over a 2-minute window. Page the on-call engineer via New Relic notification channel. Escalate to P1 if outage exceeds 5 minutes. | Logging:  Squad A/B.  Alert config: N/A |\n| Contentful entry field is null or missing | Null-safe default render: omit CTA if null, omit image if asset is missing. No uncaught exceptions. Log a warning if required fields are absent. | Log a warning with content type, entry ID, and field name to MRT log drain → New Relic Logs. Severity: warn, not error — missing optional fields indicate an authoring issue, not a system failure. | No paging alert. Warnings surfaced in a New Relic dashboard for content team review. Consider a weekly digest query if volume becomes noise. | Logging:  Squad A/B.  Dashboard: N/A |\n| Invalid HMAC on incoming webhook | Return 401 immediately. Do not process the payload. | Log with request origin IP, timestamp, and truncated payload signature to MRT log drain → New Relic Logs. | New Relic alert fires if >3 invalid HMAC requests occur within 60 seconds — treat as a potential attack. Page on-call security contact. Raise a security incident per Zimmermann IR process. | Logging:  Squad A/B.  Alert config: N/A |\n| Schema drift detected in CI gate | CI exits non-zero, blocking deploy. Developer runs npm run migrate:contentful, then re-triggers pipeline. | CI logs drift diff to GitHub Actions output. | No New Relic alert needed—CI failure signals the issue. | Squad A/B. |\n| Migration script fails mid-run | Contentful does not roll back automatically. Developer reviews partial state and writes a compensating migration. Coordinate with content editors before re-running. | Log migration step, error message, and environment to CI output. | Notify integration lead and content squad lead via Slack immediately. Do not re-trigger CI until partial state is reviewed. No New Relic alert — deploy-time failure. | Squad A/B. |\n| Preview API (CPA) accessed from browser | Architecturally impossible — CPA is MRT server-side only. If a browser request reaches CPA, the MRT proxy is misconfigured or the token leaked. | Log request origin, route, and headers to MRT log drain — severity critical. | Alert immediately on any occurrence — zero tolerance. Rotate CONTENTFUL\\_PREVIEW\\_TOKEN. Follow Zimmermann IR process. | Logging:  Squad A/B.   Alert + IR: confirm alert ownership with integration lead. Zimmermann security owns the IR process. |\n| Consent gating failure (Didomi) | Fail closed: no third-party scripts load. Affects Vimeo embeds in Contentful editorial content. See [SFCC-106](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-106). | Log Didomi initialization failure with page route to MRT log drain → New Relic Logs. | No New Relic paging alert — Didomi failures are monitored via the Didomi dashboard. Follow up with Tell No Lies / Vicky Routley per [SFCC-106](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-106). | Logging:  Squad A/B.   Monitoring: Tell No Lies / Vicky Routley. |\n\n**TODO:**\n\n* **Alert thresholds** (5% error rate, 2-minute window, >3 HMAC failures) are reasonable defaults but should be tuned once you have baseline traffic data from the first production environment.\n* **New Relic notification channel** — the alert policies reference paging on-call, but that requires a New Relic alerting channel (PagerDuty, Slack, email) to be configured. Worth calling out as a setup dependency alongside the MRT env vars checklist.\n* **MRT log drain to New Relic** — confirm the Log Centre streaming checklist item in the CDN, eCDN & Security Configuration page is complete per environment before any alert policies are wired. Prerequisite, not Squad A/B's task.\n* **Browser-layer instrumentation** — confirm whether Squad A/B is expected to add custom New Relic browser events or PWA kit instrumentation. If yes, this is new scope and needs a story.\n* **Sentry vs New Relic** — both are configured MRT env vars. Confirm with the Observability deck which owns browser-layer error reporting to avoid duplication of tooling\n\n**Environment & Locale Configuration**\n--------------------------------------\n\nThe platform uses a single Contentful Space with one Environment per delivery tier (dev → test → sit → staging → uat → production), promoted sequentially. Production uses an alias (`CONTENTFUL_ENVIRONMENT_ID=production`) for zero-downtime releases. Nine locales are configured across eight storefronts, with `en` as the default fallback. Full environment setup, alias management, and locale configuration are maintained in Contentful CMS — Setup & Operations.\n\n### Locale Rules for Content Modellers\n\n* Translatable fields (headline, body copy, CTA text, alt text) → set localized: true in the content type definition.\n* Structural fields (asset links, layout flags, product IDs) → set localized: false — shared across all locales. Canonical examples of non-localized structural fields: sfccCategoryId and sfccProductId. These are SFCC identifiers and do not vary by locale.\n* Fallback chain: if a locale (e.g. fr) has no content for a field, Contentful falls back to en automatically. Authors only fill fields they want to override.\n* Translation pipeline: Transperfect is the translation partner (HPC-006). Strategy is under discussion — Contentful squad to own.\n\n[FOR UPDATE] Handoff Boundary — Accenture vs Contentful Squad\n=============================================================\n\n*The incoming squad reads this section to know exactly where their remit starts.*\n\n|  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Concern** | **Accenture (SFCC-side) Builds** | **Incoming Contentful Squad Owns** |\n| Integration | MRT connection, CDA/CPA/webhook wiring, SSR cache, CSP | — |\n| Content types | Schema-as-code definitions + typed React components | — |\n| Environments / locales | Consume per-tier env vars | Space setup, environment/alias/locale bootstrap |\n| Content ownership | Commerce data (product/price/inventory)  All editorial (banners, modules, lookbooks, footer, navigation) | Z.immerse |\n| Translations | Responsible for all Content Ownership as outlined above | Transperfect integration, translation memory, workflow |\n| Studio Experiences | Register components in experiences module  Operate Studio visual editor; create/configure page layouts | Z.immerse Pages and Components |\n| Composed pages (PDP/PLP editorial split) | All pages outside of Z.immerse | Z.immerse pages |\n\n### One-Time Space Bootstrap Status\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Bootstrap Step** | **Status** |\n| Generate CI service account CMA token + store as CONTENTFUL\\_MANAGEMENT\\_TOKEN in GitHub Actions | ✅ Complete |\n| Bootstrap environments, locales, API keys, production alias (npm run setup:contentful) | ✅ Complete |\n| Create MRT TEST environment ([zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com](http://zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com)) | ✅ Complete |\n| Install Contentful Studio app in the space | ✅ Complete |\n| Set MRT environment variables per tier (CONTENTFUL\\_\\* + CMS\\_WEBHOOK\\_SECRET) | ⚠️ Incomplete — 4 of 9 items remaining |\n| Configure Contentful → MRT cache-purge webhook per environment (Space Settings → Webhooks) | ⚠️ Incomplete |\n| Restrict content type editing in sit/staging/uat/master to CI service account (Roles) | ⚠️ Incomplete |\n| Add CI service account CMA token as GitHub Actions secret | ✅ Complete |\n\nBlockers & Dependencies Before Squad Onboards\n=============================================\n\n|  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **#** | **Blocker / Dependency** | **Owner** | **Status** |\n| 1 | Locale count confirmed as **9** from `contentfulMapping.generated.ts` (auto-generated from live SFCC config): `en, en-US, en-GB, fr, it, es, en-CH, en-HK, en-AE`. Note: REG-005 (US-international split, updated 2026-07-10) is an active requirement that would add a 10th locale—still TBC in Business Manager and not yet in `sites.overlay.js`. Confirm with the regional config owner that REG-005 won't land before bootstrap before closing this fully. | Zimmermann | Pending confirmation on REG-005 |\n| 2 | MRT env vars per tier not set (CONTENTFUL\\_\\* + CMS\\_WEBHOOK\\_SECRET) — ops checklist item 4 | Tier-1 approver / Accenture | Incomplete |\n| 3 | Contentful → MRT cache-purge webhook not configured — ops checklist item 5 | Accenture | Incomplete |\n| 4 | Content-type editing not yet restricted to CI service account in sit/staging/uat/master — ops item 8 | Accenture | Incomplete |\n| 5 | CI service-account CMA token not added as GH Actions secret — ops item 9 | Accenture | Complete |\n| 6 | regions content-model field unconfirmed (02-contentful.md) — affects cross-storefront authoring and query-time filtering by SFCC site ID | Content strategy | Open |\n| 7 | Composed-page ownership unconfirmed: PDP/PLP editorial (Contentful vs SFCC Page Designer) and mega-menu tiles — 02-contentful.md | Tim / Content | Open |\n| 8 | Per-environment Contentful credentials to be provided to incoming squad (Space ID, CDA/CPA tokens, webhook secret) — 02-contentful.md | Contentful squad | Open |\n| 9 | Didomi purpose IDs for consent-gated components (e.g. Vimeo embeds in editorial). Blocked — pending Tell No Lies / Vicky Routley review. | Zimmermann | Blocked |\n| 10 | Contentful Enterprise plan — required for production alias (zero-downtime releases). Confirm with Zimmermann. | Zimmermann | Confirm |\n\nKey Design Decisions\n--------------------\n\n|  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Decision** | **Choice** | **Rationale** |\n| Single Contentful Space for all 8 storefronts | One Space, per-locale content fields | Locale model handles per-storefront variation. Avoids content duplication and reduces operational overhead vs one space per storefront. |\n| Schema as code — not hand-created in UI | Git-managed definitions deployed via npm run sync:contentful | Prevents schema drift, enables code review of content model changes, and gives CI visibility of structural changes before production. |\n| CDA token in browser bundle (delivery only) | Delivery API token is browser-safe | CDA tokens are read-only and scoped to one environment. Preview (CPA) and Management (CMA) tokens are never deployed to MRT or exposed to the browser. |\n| Production alias instead of fixed environment name | CONTENTFUL\\_ENVIRONMENT\\_ID=production resolves to an alias | Enables zero-downtime releases: flip the alias to a pre-tested release clone without redeploying MRT. Requires Contentful Enterprise plan. |\n| ISR cache invalidation via webhook on publish | Contentful fires HMAC-signed webhook → MRT invalidates cache | Pages are server-rendered and cached. Without cache invalidation, published content changes would not appear until cache TTL expires. Webhook makes updates near-real-time. |\n| Graceful degradation for CMS unavailability | Render page without editorial content if Contentful is down | Commerce functionality must never be blocked by CMS availability. Editorial content is an enhancement, not a dependency. |\n| Contentful SDK v11 — no connection pool isolation hook | Mitigate via graceful degradation, not pool isolation | SDK v11 does not expose a dispatcher hook for custom connection pooling. Primary mitigation is graceful degradation. |\n| SFCC ID references in Contentful content model | Plain ShortText fields (sfccProductId, sfccCategoryId), localized: false. Filtering in MRT SSR, not in the React component. | ID fields are structural, not editorial — they do not vary by locale. Resolution and conditional rendering happen entirely in the MRT SSR layer. The Contentful entry is the editorial shell; SFCC provides the commerce data it wraps. Components remain dumb and reusable. Cache keys must include the SFCC ID to avoid cross-context cache collisions. |\n\nOpen Items\n----------\n\n|  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **#** | **Item** | **Owner** | **Status** |\n| 1 | MRT environment variables: 4 of 9 variables remain unset across tiers (CONTENTFUL\\_ENVIRONMENT\\_ID, CONTENTFUL\\_DELIVERY\\_TOKEN, CONTENTFUL\\_PREVIEW\\_TOKEN, CMS\\_WEBHOOK\\_SECRET for non-dev tiers). | Accenture — Integration Lead | Incomplete |\n| 2 | Contentful → MRT cache-purge webhooks not yet configured for any environment (Space Settings → Webhooks). | Accenture — Integration Lead | Incomplete |\n| 3 | Contentful Roles: content type editing in sit/staging/uat/master must be locked to CI service account only. Not yet configured. | Accenture | Incomplete |\n| 4 | CI service account CMA token not yet added as GitHub Actions secret (CONTENTFUL\\_MANAGEMENT\\_TOKEN). | Accenture | Complete |\n| 5 | Sprint 1 & 2 content type list — resolved via Jira backlog analysis. Requires confirmation from incoming Contentful squad before build begins. | Squad-A + Contentful Squad | Pending Confirmation |\n| 6 | Transperfect translation integration strategy (HPC-006) — workflow and translation memory approach TBD. | Zimmermann / Contentful Squad | Open |\n| 7 | Didomi purpose IDs — required to gate consent-relevant Contentful components (e.g. Vimeo embeds). Blocked pending Tell No Lies / Vicky Routley review. | Zimmermann | Blocked |\n| 8 | Contentful Enterprise plan — required for production alias. Confirm Zimmermann account is on Enterprise before first production release. | Zimmermann | Confirm |\n| 9 | Z.immerse component scope (SFCC-10) — full list of editorial components not yet defined. Pending Accenture design Figma delivery and Zimmermann sign-off. Target Sprint 5. | Accenture Design + Zimmermann | Open |\n\nOwnership Boundary & SFCC Build Scope\n-------------------------------------\n\n### Ownership Boundary\n\n|  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Area** | **Owner** | **Detail** |\n| Contentful space provisioning & billing | Zimmermann | Zimmermann owns the Contentful account and space. |\n| Content type definitions (schema as code) | Accenture (Squad-A) + Contentful Squad | Initial types defined by Accenture for Sprint 1 & 2; Contentful squad expands from there. |\n| Content authoring & entry management | Contentful Squad / Zimmermann | No Accenture involvement post-handoff. |\n| Translation integration (Transperfect) | Contentful Squad | Out of Accenture scope. |\n| PWA components rendering Contentful content | Accenture (Squad-A) | React components in overrides/. Each content type needs a typed React component. |\n| Contentful SDK integration in PWA | Accenture (Squad-A) | contentful v11 SDK, SSR fetching, ISR cache invalidation, graceful degradation. |\n| Cache-purge webhook receiver (MRT) | Accenture (Squad-A) | HMAC-verified webhook endpoint in the MRT Node layer. |\n| Studio Experiences / visual editor | Accenture sets up; Contentful Squad operates | Accenture registers components; Contentful squad uses the Studio editor. |\n| Environment provisioning & alias management | Accenture (initial); Contentful Squad (ongoing) | npm run setup:contentful once, then Contentful squad takes over. |\n| CI/CD Contentful pipeline | Accenture (Squad-A) | npm run migrate:contentful in CI. Drift detection gates. |\n| Contentful Roles & permissions | Accenture (initial setup) | Restrict content type editing on sit/staging/uat/master to CI service account only. |\n\n### Accenture Build Checklist\n\n### Infrastructure & Auth\n\n1977\n1aa1fb90-3a9a-4d95-8eb3-3821d3026823\ncomplete\nCreate CI service account, invite as Space Administrator, generate CMA token, store as CONTENTFUL\\_MANAGEMENT\\_TOKEN in GitHub Actions.\n\n1978\n2bb47d5f-a17a-4764-9a5d-7065673d71d5\nincomplete\nRun npm run setup:contentful — bootstraps environments, locales, API keys, production alias.\n\n1979\n2930f515-2067-4339-b79a-f4a136f30e14\nincomplete\nSet all MRT environment variables per tier\n\n1980\nbf79125d-ce72-44e0-8bad-200e2e066dc7\nincomplete\nConfigure Contentful roles: lock content type editing in sit/staging/uat/master to CI service account.\n\n1996\n912f0ed1-17ac-47a3-8d6c-84a4f7a6e35b\nincomplete\nConfigure MRT log drain per environment and verify log ingestion in New Relic before wiring alert policies. *Only if we’ll use NewRelic as our monitoring tool*\n\n### PWA Integration\n\n1981\nc370467a-7f61-4193-a4bb-3386f5a51d4e\nincomplete\nIntegrate Contentful SDK (contentful v11). Configure SSR fetching via CDA.\n\n1982\n8bbf8bcc-4bcc-4be9-be8d-2b4942d29f1a\nincomplete\nImplement Preview API proxy (MRT server-side). CPA token never reaches browser.\n\n1983\nb2fb102a-5842-4908-907a-483da2b845b8\nincomplete\nImplement HMAC-verified cache-purge webhook receiver in MRT Node layer.\n\n1984\n4408af84-abb1-4bce-a6ae-887eaf590145\nincomplete\nImplement graceful degradation: if Contentful is down, render page without editorial content.\n\n### Content Type Infrastructure\n\n1985\n204ade8e-c9ef-479f-b1d8-d8dbcc2bd59c\nincomplete\nWrite content type definitions for all Sprint 1 & 2 types in scripts/contentful/content-types/\\*.js.\n\n1986\n80e67107-a194-46a5-aa4f-031f57118fcd\nincomplete\nWrite corresponding TypeScript React components in overrides/ for each type using field mappings \n\n1987\n895ea869-e755-42dc-80c4-8e3aaa34888a\nincomplete\nRegister Studio Experience components in the experiences registration module.\n\n1988\ne8a0112d-1917-4a21-ae51-338d2d43c0f8\nincomplete\nWire npm run sync:contentful, npm run migrate:contentful, and npm run detect:drift into CI.\n\n### Webhooks & Cache\n\n1989\nc0745c98-35db-4567-b989-b1065bcbcc0d\nincomplete\nConfigure Contentful → MRT cache-purge webhook per environment (Space Settings → Webhooks).\n\n1990\n278e62bf-0b40-4656-9f9c-fefc1f6342e6\nincomplete\nCreate MRT TEST environment: [zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com](http://zimmermann-test.sfdc-8tgtt5-ecom1.exp-delivery.com).\n\n### Handoff Artifacts to Contentful Squad\n\n1991\nec0c72c3-4a22-4ffe-b637-8334a75f036f\nincomplete\nThis TSD document.\n\n1992\n8695e827-0a25-4e23-90b9-1f176a53bd25\nincomplete\nContent type definitions deployed to dev environment.\n\n1993\n042eb937-7e2a-4ab7-ac60-b27153b36185\nincomplete\nContentful environment URLs and credentials per tier.\n\n1994\nfab59db0-dbb3-4f5a-ac8b-9e70dfa9c4a8\nincomplete\nLocale configuration confirmation (9 locales, matching SFCC sites.js).\n\n1995\nb0167af6-b483-4138-9319-981a1d487a04\nincomplete\nCI/CD pipeline documentation showing where migration and drift steps run.\n\nRelated TSDs & References\n-------------------------\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Resource** | **URL / Location** |\n| .docs/integration/02-contentful.md (primary technical source) | zimmermann-pwa/.docs/integration/02-contentful.md |\n| Contentful CMS — Setup & Operations (Confluence) | Contentful CMS — Setup & Operations |\n| Technical Solution Design – PWA (Confluence) | Technical Solution Design – PWA |\n| TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration (Confluence) | TSD: Product — SFCC Catalogue & Data Integration |\n| 04.1.1 Homepage and Content Requirements (Confluence) | 04.1.1 Homepage and Content |\n| 04.5 Storefronts (Confluence) | 04.5 Storefronts |\n| Technical Environment Setup (Confluence) | Technical Environment Setup |\n| SFCC-249 Jira Ticket (Current Spike) | SFCC-24990f39d3a-944a-3fa5-a6e7-595259a51237System Jira |\n| SFCC-123 Jira Ticket (Original Spike, Done) | SFCC-12390f39d3a-944a-3fa5-a6e7-595259a51237System Jira |\n| Contentful Delivery API docs | <https://www.contentful.com/developers/docs/references/content-delivery-api/> |\n| Contentful Management API docs | <https://www.contentful.com/developers/docs/references/content-management-api/> |\n| MRT Application Architecture Strategy (SFCC-237) | [SFCC-237](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-237) — TSD in progress. TODO: Link TSD here once complete. |",
